<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Jan registered soybean exports 2.35 mln tns.</title>
<headline>Brazil Jan registered soybean exports 2.35 mln tns.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil registered 2.35 million tonnes of soybeans from the 1997/98 harvest for export by Jan 30, according to Commerce Department figures published by independent consultants Safras e Mercado.</p>
<p>This represented 40 percent of the total 5.8 million tonnes forecast to be exported this year, up from 34 percent at the same time last year, Safras said.</p>
<p>Export registration figures, in thousands of tonnes, were as follows:</p>
<p>						 97/98	 96/97</p>
<p> SOYBEANS Registered (A)		 2347.1	1234.9</p>
<p> Forecast exports (B)		    5800.0	3620.0</p>
<p> A/B					   40 pct	34 pct</p>
<p> SOYMEAL Registered (A)		  2153.1	1954.6</p>
<p> Forecast exports (B)		   10150.0     10900.0</p>
<p> A/B					   21 pct	18 pct</p>
<p> SOYOIL Registered (A)		    325.9	 305.5</p>
<p> Forecast exports (B)		    1280.0	1300.0</p>
<p> A/B					   25 pct	24 pct</p>
<p>--Joelle Diderich, Sao Paulo newsroom +55 11 248 5417</p>
</text>
